# Migrating Flat Pulumi TypeScript to ComponentResource with Aliases

Here's a complete migration pattern for your canonical scenario, preventing resource replacement through proper `aliases` usage.

## Core Pattern

When refactoring flat Pulumi code into ComponentResources, resources get new URNs. Use `aliases` to tell Pulumi these are the same physical cloud resources.

## File Structure (Post-Migration)

```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── storage.ts
│   ├── database.ts
│   ├── iam.ts
│   ├── compute.ts
│   └── networking.ts
└── index.ts
dev.yaml
prod.yaml
```

## Implementation

### 1. StorageComponent

```typescript
// src/components/storage.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";

export interface StorageComponentArgs {
    environment: "dev" | "prod";
}

export class StorageComponent extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public bucket: aws.s3.Bucket;

    constructor(
        name: string,
        args: StorageComponentArgs,
        opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions
    ) {
        super("custom:storage:StorageComponent", name, {}, opts);

        this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(
            "app-assets",
            {
                versioning: { enabled: true },
                serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: {
                    rule: {
                        applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: {
                            sseAlgorithm: "AES256",
                        },
                    },
                },
                blockPublicAcls: true,
                blockPublicPolicy: true,
                ignorePublicAcls: true,
                restrictPublicBuckets: true,
                // Prod: cross-region replication to us-west-2
                ...(args.environment === "prod" && {
                    replicationConfiguration: {
                        role: new aws.iam.Role("replication-role", {
                            assumeRolePolicy: pulumi.jsonStringify({
                                Version: "2012-10-17",
                                Statement: [{
                                    Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
                                    Effect: "Allow",
                                    Principal: { Service: "s3.amazonaws.com" },
                                }],
                            }),
                        }, { parent: this }).arn,
                        rules: [{
                            id: "replicate-all",
                            status: "Enabled",
                            priority: 1,
                            destination: {
                                bucket: `arn:aws:s3:::app-assets-replica-us-west-2`,
                                replicationTime: { status: "Enabled", time: 15 },
                                metrics: { status: "Enabled", eventThreshold: 15 },
                            },
                        }],
                    },
                }),
            },
            {
                parent: this,
                // Map old flat resource URN to new component-scoped resource
                aliases: [{ name: "app-assets" }],
            }
        );

        this.registerOutputs();
    }
}
```

### 2. DatabaseComponent

```typescript
// src/components/database.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";

export interface DatabaseComponentArgs {
    environment: "dev" | "prod";
}

export class DatabaseComponent extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public instance: aws.rds.Instance;

    constructor(
        name: string,
        args: DatabaseComponentArgs,
        opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions
    ) {
        super("custom:database:DatabaseComponent", name, {}, opts);

        const config = {
            dev: {
                instanceClass: "db.t3.micro",
                multiAz: false,
                allocatedStorage: 20,
                backupRetention: 3,
            },
            prod: {
                instanceClass: "db.t3.medium",
                multiAz: true,
                allocatedStorage: 100,
                backupRetention: 7,
            },
        }[args.environment];

        this.instance = new aws.rds.Instance(
            "postgres",
            {
                instanceClass: config.instanceClass,
                engine: "postgres",
                engineVersion: "14",
                databaseName: "appdb",
                username: "appuser",
                password: new pulumi.Config().requireSecret("db-password"),
                allocatedStorage: config.allocatedStorage,
                storageEncrypted: true,
                multiAz: config.multiAz,
                backupRetentionPeriod: config.backupRetention,
                deletionProtection: args.environment === "prod",
                publiclyAccessible: false,
                skipFinalSnapshot: args.environment === "dev",
                parameterGroupName: new aws.rds.ParameterGroup(
                    "pg14-params",
                    { family: "postgres14" },
                    { parent: this }
                ).name,
            },
            {
                parent: this,
                aliases: [{ name: "postgres" }],
            }
        );

        this.registerOutputs();
    }
}
```

### 3. IamComponent

```typescript
// src/components/iam.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";

export interface IamComponentArgs {
    environment: "dev" | "prod";
}

export class IamComponent extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public user: aws.iam.User;
    public role: aws.iam.Role;
    public accessKey: aws.iam.AccessKey;

    constructor(
        name: string,
        args: IamComponentArgs,
        opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions
    ) {
        super("custom:iam:IamComponent", name, {}, opts);

        this.user = new aws.iam.User(
            "service-account",
            { name: `app-service-${args.environment}` },
            { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "service-account" }] }
        );

        const assumeRolePolicy = pulumi.jsonStringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [
                {
                    Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
                    Effect: "Allow",
                    Principal:
                        args.environment === "prod"
                            ? {
                                Federated: pulumi.concat(
                                    "arn:aws:iam::",
                                    aws.getCallerIdentity().accountId,
                                    ":oidc-provider/oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLK7S7FCC4D04E1B5C6E"
                                ),
                            }
                            : { AWS: this.user.arn },
                },
            ],
        });

        this.role = new aws.iam.Role(
            "app-role",
            { assumeRolePolicy },
            {
                parent: this,
                aliases: [{ name: "app-role" }],
            }
        );

        // Prod: minimal policy; dev: broader for testing
        const policy = new aws.iam.RolePolicy(
            "app-policy",
            {
                role: this.role.id,
                policy: pulumi.jsonStringify({
                    Version: "2012-10-17",
                    Statement: [
                        {
                            Action: args.environment === "prod"
                                ? ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"]
                                : "s3:*",
                            Effect: "Allow",
                            Resource: "*",
                        },
                        {
                            Action: args.environment === "prod"
                                ? ["rds-db:connect"]
                                : ["rds:*"],
                            Effect: "Allow",
                            Resource: "*",
                        },
                    ],
                }),
            },
            { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "app-policy" }] }
        );

        this.accessKey = new aws.iam.AccessKey(
            "service-key",
            { user: this.user.name },
            { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "service-key" }] }
        );

        this.registerOutputs({
            roleArn: this.role.arn,
            accessKeyId: this.accessKey.id,
        });
    }
}
```

### 4. ComputeComponent (EKS)

```typescript
// src/components/compute.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";

export interface ComputeComponentArgs {
    environment: "dev" | "prod";
    vpcId: pulumi.Input<string>;
    subnetIds: pulumi.Input<string>[];
}

export class ComputeComponent extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public cluster: eks.Cluster;

    constructor(
        name: string,
        args: ComputeComponentArgs,
        opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions
    ) {
        super("custom:compute:ComputeComponent", name, {}, opts);

        const config = {
            dev: { nodeCount: 2, instanceType: "t3.medium" },
            prod: { nodeCount: 4, instanceType: "t3.large" },
        }[args.environment];

        this.cluster = new eks.Cluster(
            "app-cluster",
            {
                vpcId: args.vpcId,
                subnetIds: args.subnetIds,
                desiredCapacity: config.nodeCount,
                minSize: config.nodeCount,
                maxSize: args.environment === "prod" ? 8 : 4,
                instanceType: config.instanceType,
                enabledClusterLogTypes: ["api", "audit"],
                encryptionConfig: { resources: ["secrets"], provider: { keyArn: "" } },
            },
            { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "app-cluster" }] }
        );

        this.registerOutputs({
            kubeconfig: this.cluster.kubeconfig,
        });
    }
}
```

### 5. NetworkingComponent

```typescript
// src/components/networking.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";

export interface NetworkingComponentArgs {
    environment: "dev" | "prod";
    targetGroupArn?: pulumi.Input<string>;
}

export class NetworkingComponent extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public loadBalancer: aws.lb.LoadBalancer | aws.cloudfront.Distribution;
    public listener: aws.lb.Listener | undefined;

    constructor(
        name: string,
        args: NetworkingComponentArgs,
        opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions
    ) {
        super("custom:networking:NetworkingComponent", name, {}, opts);

        if (args.environment === "dev") {
            // Dev: internal ALB
            this.loadBalancer = new aws.lb.LoadBalancer(
                "app-alb",
                {
                    internal: true,
                    loadBalancerType: "application",
                },
                { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "app-alb" }] }
            );

            this.listener = new aws.lb.Listener(
                "https-listener",
                {
                    loadBalancerArn: this.loadBalancer.arn,
                    protocol: "HTTPS",
                    port: 443,
                    defaultActions: [{
                        type: "forward",
                        targetGroupArn: args.targetGroupArn!,
                    }],
                    certificateArn: new pulumi.Config().require(
                        "certificate-arn"
                    ),
                },
                { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "https-listener" }] }
            );
        } else {
            // Prod: CloudFront + ACM
            const oai = new aws.cloudfront.OriginAccessIdentity(
                "oai",
                { comment: "OAI for app assets" },
                { parent: this }
            );

            this.loadBalancer = new aws.cloudfront.Distribution(
                "cdn",
                {
                    enabled: true,
                    isIpv6Enabled: true,
                    origins: [
                        {
                            domainName: args.targetGroupArn || "example.com",
                            originId: "app-origin",
                        },
                    ],
                    defaultCacheBehavior: {
                        allowedMethods: [
                            "GET",
                            "HEAD",
                            "DELETE",
                            "OPTIONS",
                            "PATCH",
                            "POST",
                            "PUT",
                        ],
                        cachedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD"],
                        targetOriginId: "app-origin",
                        forwardedValues: {
                            queryString: true,
                            cookies: { forward: "all" },
                            headers: ["*"],
                        },
                        viewerProtocolPolicy: "redirect-to-https",
                        minTtl: 0,
                        defaultTtl: 0,
                        maxTtl: 0,
                    },
                    restrictions: { geoRestriction: { restrictionType: "none" } },
                    viewerCertificate: {
                        acmCertificateArn: new pulumi.Config().require(
                            "certificate-arn"
                        ),
                        sslSupportMethod: "sni-only",
                        minimumProtocolVersion: "TLSv1.2_2021",
                    },
                },
                { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "cdn" }] }
            );
        }

        this.registerOutputs();
    }
}
```

### 6. Main Index

```typescript
// src/index.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import { StorageComponent } from "./components/storage";
import { DatabaseComponent } from "./components/database";
import { IamComponent } from "./components/iam";
import { ComputeComponent } from "./components/compute";
import { NetworkingComponent } from "./components/networking";

const config = new pulumi.Config();
const environment = config.require("environment") as "dev" | "prod";

// VPC (assume existing or create here)
const vpc = new aws.ec2.Vpc("app-vpc", {
    cidrBlock: "10.0.0.0/16",
});

const subnets = [
    new aws.ec2.Subnet("subnet-1", { vpcId: vpc.id, cidrBlock: "10.0.1.0/24" }),
    new aws.ec2.Subnet("subnet-2", { vpcId: vpc.id, cidrBlock: "10.0.2.0/24" }),
];

// Instantiate components
const storage = new StorageComponent(`storage`, { environment });
const database = new DatabaseComponent(`database`, { environment });
const iam = new IamComponent(`iam`, { environment });
const compute = new ComputeComponent(`compute`, {
    environment,
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    subnetIds: subnets.map(s => s.id),
});
const networking = new NetworkingComponent(`networking`, {
    environment,
    targetGroupArn: "arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-east-1:ACCOUNT:targetgroup/app/*",
});

// Exports
export const bucketName = storage.bucket.id;
export const dbEndpoint = database.instance.endpoint;
export const roleArn = iam.role.arn;
export const clusterName = compute.cluster.core.cluster.name;
export const loadBalancerDns =
    networking.loadBalancer instanceof aws.lb.LoadBalancer
        ? networking.loadBalancer.dnsName
        : networking.loadBalancer.domainName;
```

### 7. Stack Configuration

```yaml
# dev.yaml
config:
  environment: dev
  aws:region: us-east-1
  certificate-arn: arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:ACCOUNT:certificate/dev-cert
  db-password:
    secure: AAABAxxxxx  # pulumi config set --secret

# prod.yaml
config:
  environment: prod
  aws:region: us-east-1
  certificate-arn: arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:ACCOUNT:certificate/prod-cert
  db-password:
    secure: AAABAyyyyy
```

## Migration Workflow

```bash
# 1. Export current state (check resource URNs)
pulumi stack export > pre-migration.json

# 2. Refactor code (add ComponentResources with aliases)
# (copy code above)

# 3. Preview changes (should show no replacements)
pulumi preview

# 4. If preview shows "*Replace*", adjust aliases:
#    - Verify names match old flat resource names exactly
#    - Check parent: this is set on all aliased resources
#    - Re-run preview

# 5. Apply when safe
pulumi up

# 6. Verify (compare state URNs)
pulumi stack export > post-migration.json
```

## Critical Rules

| Rule | Why | Example |
|------|-----|---------|
| **Alias name must match old resource name exactly** | URN includes name path | Old: `aws:s3/bucket:Bucket::app-assets` → `aliases: [{ name: "app-assets" }]` |
| **Set `parent: this` on all aliased resources** | Parent path is part of URN | Without it, URN becomes `...::StorageComponent$app-assets`, not matching |
| **One alias per old resource** | Deduplication | Don't alias same resource twice in different components |
| **Aliases only adopt; don't rename** | They prevent replacement, not drift | If you rename a resource without alias, it will be replaced |
| **Test in dev stack first** | Catch errors early | Always migrate dev before prod |

## Troubleshooting

If `pulumi preview` shows `*Replace*`:

1. **Check URN mismatch**: `pulumi stack export | grep "urn:"` to see old URNs
2. **Verify name path**: `old-name` in flat != `parent$old-name` in component → fix alias
3. **Missing parent**: Ensure all aliased resources have `parent: this`
4. **Wrong parent type**: Don't mix ComponentResource with Resource; use super() consistently

This pattern scales to your prod environment—no code changes needed, only stack config (`prod.yaml`) with different sizing and region.
